                         ============================================= -->
                    <div class="faq-section scroll-reveal">

                        <h4>
                            For Trainees (Interns / Seekers)
                        </h4>


                        <h4>
                            I. What is 1trainee.com Internship Portal?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            The Internship Portal is a platform designed to
                            connect students, recent graduates, PGs and
                            research scholars with internship / fellowship
                            opportunities across various industries
                            nationally & internationally.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            It allows trainees to browse, apply for
                            internships / live projects, and manage their
                            applications & responses in one place.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            II. How do I register on the portal?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            To register, click on the "Sign Up" button on
                            the homepage and add details, fill in your
                            personal details from profile option available
                            in dashboard with educational background, and
                            upload your resume.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            After submitting, you will receive a confirmation
                            email with login details of your account.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            III. How can I search for internships?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            Once logged in, use the search bar to enter
                            keywords related to your interests, such as
                            internship / job titles or companies.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            You can also filter internships by location,
                            industry, and duration. Do not forget to create
                            your profile from the dashboard.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            IV. How do I apply for an internship?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            After finding a suitable internship, click on
                            the internship / job listing to view details.
                            If you want to apply, click the "Apply Now"
                            button, fill out any required fields, and
                            submit your application.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            V. Can I edit my profile after registration?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            Yes, you can update your profile by going to the
                            "Profile" section. Here you can modify your
                            personal information, resume details like
                            hobbies, languages, contact information,
                            references and skills.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            VI. How will I be notified about internship applications?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            You will receive email notifications about the
                            status of your application including interview
                            invitations and other notices.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            You can also check the "Application Status -
                            Applied" section on your dashboard.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            VII. Is there a fee to use the portal?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            The portal is free for trainees to use. There
                            are no charges for applying to internships or
                            using any features of the platform.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Resume building facility gives you more than
                            35 design options and no charges are applied
                            on this. You can download and use them.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            VIII. What should I do if I forget my password?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            On the login page, click the
                            "Forgot Password" link. Enter your registered
                            email address, and you will receive instructions
                            to reset your password.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            IX. How can I get support if I encounter issues?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            If you experience any problems, visit the
                            "Help" section on the portal or contact our
                            support team via email at
                            contact@kavin.co.za / contact@1trainee.com.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            X. What are the responsibilities of the intern?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            Interns are expected to follow company policies,
                            complete assigned tasks, seek feedback, and
                            communicate any challenges they encounter.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            XI. Can internships be offered remotely?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            Yes, many companies offer remote internships.
                            It is important to specify this in the internship
                            posting and ensure that the necessary tools and
                            support are available.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            XII. What happens if an intern faces issues while
                            on the internship?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            Interns should report any issues to their
                            supervisor or designated contact at the company.
                            We also provide resources and support for
                            conflict resolution.
                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <!-- =============================================
                         ORGANIZATIONS
                         ============================================= -->
                    <div class="faq-section scroll-reveal">

                        <h4>
                            For Organizations (Recruiters)
                        </h4>


                        <h4>
                            1. How do I create an employer (Recruiter) account?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            To create an account, click on the "Sign Up"
                            button for recruiters, fill in your company
                            details, and create a profile.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            You will be sent a confirmation mail with
                            login details.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            2. How can I post an internship opportunity?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            Log in to your recruiter account, go to the
                            "Post an internship" section, and fill out
                            the internship details, including job
                            description, requirements, and application
                            deadlines.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            3. Can I view applications for my internship postings?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            Yes, you can view and manage all applications
                            through the "Manage Applications" section on
                            your dashboard.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            4. How can I communicate with applicants?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            You can communicate with applicants via their
                            provided contact details.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            5. Is there a fee to post internship opportunities?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            The portal is free for organizations to use.
                            There are no charges to post internships or
                            using any features of the platform.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            6. Can I edit or remove an internship job listing?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            Yes, you can edit or remove a job listing from
                            the "Edit" section. You can update the job
                            details or withdraw the posting if it is no
                            longer available.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            7. How do I track the performance of my job postings?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            The portal provides analytics on job postings,
                            including views, applications received, and
                            other relevant metrics.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            8. What should I do if I have trouble using the portal?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            If you encounter any issues, visit the
                            "Contact" section for troubleshooting tips or
                            contact our support team.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            9. How do I cancel my employer / recruiter account?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            To cancel your account, contact our support
                            team. They will guide you through the account
                            closure process.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            10. How can we promote diversity and inclusion
                            in our internship programs?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            Companies can actively seek applicants from
                            diverse backgrounds, provide training on
                            inclusivity, and foster an environment that
                            values different perspectives.
                        </p>


                        <h4>
                            11. Who can we contact for more information?
                        </h4>

                        <p>
                            For any questions or additional information,
                            companies can reach out to our support team
                            via email or through the contact form on our
                            website.
                        </p>

                    </div>


